1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:09,130
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:11,345
[Victor speaking indistinctly]

3
00:00:11,428 --> 00:00:12,596
[tech] <i>Where are you?</i>

4
00:00:19,102 --> 00:00:21,522
[laughs]

5
00:00:21,605 --> 00:00:22,981
- [gasps]
- [Victor] Troy?

6
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:27,444
- [panting]
- [Victor, muffled] Troy?

7
00:00:27,528 --> 00:00:28,820
Keep breathing, buddy.

8
00:00:29,821 --> 00:00:31,782
Keep breathing. Look up at me.

9
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:35,869
Keep breathing. You're okay.

10
00:00:36,787 --> 00:00:38,705
Keep breathing, Troy. There you go.

11
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:41,416
[normal audio] Try to breathe.
Try to breathe.

12
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,293
- Okay. Okay.
- [chokes]

13
00:00:43,377 --> 00:00:45,337
Easy. Can you hear me?

14
00:00:45,838 --> 00:00:48,674
Okay. We had to rapid-sequence you,
I'm sorry.

15
00:00:49,341 --> 00:00:50,425
Sir.

16
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:52,052
Oh, fuck. Yes.

17
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:54,179
Listen, your core temperature is lagging.

18
00:00:54,263 --> 00:00:56,473
We're gonna administer
a thermal flush, okay?

19
00:00:56,557 --> 00:00:57,558
How...

20
00:00:59,643 --> 00:01:00,644
How long?

21
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:01,895
Seven years.

22
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:04,105
- [panting]
- Come on. Bite down.

23
00:01:05,691 --> 00:01:07,609
All right, there it goes.

24
00:01:10,112 --> 00:01:13,490
Okay. Here we go. Here it comes.
Here it comes. Here it comes.

25
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:16,451
There you go. Okay. Okay.

26
00:01:17,286 --> 00:01:18,704
- [grunting]
- Grab his legs.

27
00:01:18,787 --> 00:01:21,331
- Easy.
- [groaning]

28
00:01:21,874 --> 00:01:22,875
[Victor] Grab his legs.

29
00:02:18,472 --> 00:02:20,015
How'd you sleep?

30
00:02:20,098 --> 00:02:22,809
[Daniel] It's not the sleep.
It's the waking up.

31
00:02:22,893 --> 00:02:24,520
I know, I'm sorry. Here you go.

32
00:02:24,603 --> 00:02:26,396
[groans]

33
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:29,274
- There's gotta be a better way.
- We'll work on that.

34
00:02:32,611 --> 00:02:35,072
- This was recorded a couple days ago.
- [beeps]

35
00:02:35,739 --> 00:02:37,699
[The Algorithm] <i>Why are you in the Vault?</i>

36
00:02:37,783 --> 00:02:39,910
[Jimmy] <i>Dad sent me here. He said--</i>

37
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:41,370
[The Algorithm] <i>What is your name?</i>

38
00:02:42,913 --> 00:02:43,914
[Jimmy] <i>Jimmy.</i>

39
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:46,708
[The Algorithm] <i>Your father
is Russell Conroy, head of IT.</i>

40
00:02:46,792 --> 00:02:47,876
Which silo?

41
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,044
[Jimmy] <i>Mm-hmm.</i>

42
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:51,547
[The Algorithm]
<i>What did he tell you, Jimmy?</i>

43
00:02:52,589 --> 00:02:54,716
[Jimmy] <i>Don't let anybody in
no matter what.</i>

44
00:02:55,926 --> 00:02:57,636
[The Algorithm]
<i>Is there an adult with you?</i>

45
00:02:58,303 --> 00:03:02,641
[Jimmy] <i>Solo brought me here,
but he-he went back to fight the rebels.</i>

46
00:03:05,102 --> 00:03:06,144
Which silo?

47
00:03:06,228 --> 00:03:07,271
Seventeen.

48
00:03:07,855 --> 00:03:10,899
It started with a failed cleaning,
got worse when he went out of sight.

49
00:03:10,983 --> 00:03:13,277
They thought it was safe to go outside.

50
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:16,488
Yeah. Rebellion was led by the sheriff.

51
00:03:16,989 --> 00:03:20,659
We think the shadow blew the bridge
to keep them out of IT,

52
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:22,536
but somehow the sheriff got across.

53
00:03:23,412 --> 00:03:26,582
He took the head of IT, the kid's father,
to the Vault

54
00:03:26,665 --> 00:03:31,211
and threatened to blow his brains out
if his kid didn't open the door.

55
00:03:34,923 --> 00:03:36,175
He didn't open the door.

56
00:03:36,967 --> 00:03:38,010
Fuck.

57
00:03:38,719 --> 00:03:40,095
- Yeah.
- When was that?

58
00:03:40,179 --> 00:03:41,263
Two hours ago.

59
00:03:41,346 --> 00:03:43,473
Any part of that triggers the Safeguard.

60
00:03:43,557 --> 00:03:46,935
A Safeguard was attempted,
but the compound couldn't be delivered.

61
00:03:47,019 --> 00:03:49,563
[stammers] There's no pressure drop
in the line.

62
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:52,274
We haven't determined
whether it was a mechanical failure, or--

63
00:03:52,357 --> 00:03:54,818
Or they found the delivery pipe
and disabled it.

64
00:03:54,902 --> 00:03:56,528
- Yeah.
- That happened once before.

65
00:03:58,155 --> 00:04:00,657
In either case,
we need a different outcome this time.

66
00:04:00,741 --> 00:04:01,825
That's why I'm here.

67
00:04:01,909 --> 00:04:03,202
Exactly.

68
00:04:03,285 --> 00:04:04,411
[sighs]

69
00:04:05,537 --> 00:04:06,997
You okay?

70
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,332
[clears throat]

71
00:04:08,415 --> 00:04:09,625
Yeah.

72
00:04:09,708 --> 00:04:11,043
Do we have eyes in the sky?

73
00:04:11,126 --> 00:04:12,669
Operations have a drone up.

74
00:04:13,545 --> 00:04:15,547
- [people muttering]
- [devices beeping]

75
00:04:18,716 --> 00:04:19,927
Anything?

76
00:04:20,010 --> 00:04:21,220
[commander] Nothing yet.

77
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:26,183
Troy, this is Susan,
our senior drone commander on shift.

78
00:04:29,061 --> 00:04:30,395
What's your payload?

79
00:04:30,479 --> 00:04:33,524
Thirty liters of compound,
2,000 rounds of ordnance.

80
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:44,993
[typing]

81
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:48,205
- [Charlotte speaks indistinctly]
- [Victor] I'm not sure about that.

82
00:04:56,505 --> 00:04:58,549
[alarm blaring]

83
00:04:59,383 --> 00:05:02,094
[Charlotte] Sir, Silo 17 doors opening.

84
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:05,180
[people murmuring]

85
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:11,895
Oh, no, no.

86
00:05:11,979 --> 00:05:13,981
[silo citizens cheering]

87
00:05:28,495 --> 00:05:29,663
Awaiting your order.

88
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:36,753
Troy.

89
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:42,050
Let's not do anything. Just not yet.

90
00:05:42,134 --> 00:05:45,137
The longer they're outside, the greater
the risk of contact with another silo.

91
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:47,514
Look, let's figure out a way
to get them back inside.

92
00:05:47,598 --> 00:05:49,641
We'll run a line
through the Forward Vault door.

93
00:05:49,725 --> 00:05:51,393
We'll Safeguard them that way.

94
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:54,104
Their groundwater pump is out.
It's flooded past the generator.

95
00:05:54,188 --> 00:05:55,689
We can't use the Forward Vault doors.

96
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:56,982
- Susan.
- Hmm?

97
00:05:57,065 --> 00:06:00,194
Let's get all the techs out of these seats
and scramble all available pilots.

98
00:06:00,277 --> 00:06:03,906
And let's get drones in the air.
Ten with ordnance. Twenty with compound.

99
00:06:04,823 --> 00:06:08,035
Keep them high enough
that the fugitives won't see or hear them.

100
00:06:08,118 --> 00:06:09,494
Unless someone goes over the berm,

101
00:06:09,578 --> 00:06:12,206
don't alert me
until there are 9,500 fugitives.

102
00:06:12,289 --> 00:06:13,332
I need to eat.

103
00:06:13,832 --> 00:06:15,751
[cheering continues]

104
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,405
[Daniel] God, this stuff's crap.

105
00:06:46,573 --> 00:06:49,076
I know. And such small portions.

106
00:06:51,161 --> 00:06:52,162
Uh-huh.

107
00:06:52,871 --> 00:06:53,914
That old joke.

108
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,298
I'm not sure about this.

109
00:07:03,382 --> 00:07:05,551
Safeguarding them inside isn't
an option anymore.

110
00:07:05,634 --> 00:07:08,303
By going outside,
they've given us a second chance.

111
00:07:08,387 --> 00:07:11,890
Safeguards happen underground,
inside a silo.

112
00:07:13,684 --> 00:07:14,768
They're antiseptic.

113
00:07:15,269 --> 00:07:19,398
If we do what you're thinking,
this amounts to an out-of-silo Safeguard.

114
00:07:19,982 --> 00:07:22,317
The deaths are going to be visceral.

115
00:07:22,401 --> 00:07:24,528
- Out in the open.
- I don't see that we have a choice.

116
00:07:24,611 --> 00:07:26,446
We don't know how our people will react.

117
00:07:26,530 --> 00:07:30,868
I'm concerned about the potential effects
of trauma on morale and mission-readiness.

118
00:07:30,951 --> 00:07:35,330
The top priority, per the Directive,
is to prevent contamination between silos.

119
00:07:35,414 --> 00:07:36,540
I understand that.

120
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:38,166
- No, what?
- That's not what I'm saying.

121
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:39,459
Everything depends on that.

122
00:07:39,543 --> 00:07:41,879
- That's not what I'm--
- Excuse me, sir.

123
00:07:41,962 --> 00:07:43,172
Fugitives on the berm.

124
00:07:43,255 --> 00:07:44,715
Oh, fuck.

125
00:07:45,424 --> 00:07:47,259
Hey, I'll look after your pilots.

126
00:07:47,342 --> 00:07:48,343
I promise.

127
00:07:48,427 --> 00:07:49,428
Okay.

128
00:08:17,164 --> 00:08:19,291
[Charlotte] Jenkins, eyes on the sheriff.

129
00:08:38,977 --> 00:08:40,312
[Daniel] How many fugitives?

130
00:08:41,395 --> 00:08:43,857
9,832.

131
00:08:46,026 --> 00:08:47,444
Here's the order of operations.

132
00:08:47,945 --> 00:08:50,447
Group 1 will engage
the sheriff and his family.

133
00:08:51,198 --> 00:08:54,743
Group 2 will administer compound
at the ramp to prevent reentrance.

134
00:08:55,619 --> 00:08:58,413
3 and 4 will fly interlaced coverage

135
00:08:58,497 --> 00:09:00,874
until the target area is saturated
with compound.

136
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:04,711
Groups 5 and 6 will engage targets
on command. Got it?

137
00:09:04,795 --> 00:09:07,047
- [pilots] Yes, sir.
- Good. Begin.

138
00:09:12,970 --> 00:09:14,930
- Groups, report.
- Group 1, ready.

139
00:09:15,013 --> 00:09:16,932
2, ready.

140
00:09:17,015 --> 00:09:18,559
- 3, ready.
- 4, ready.

141
00:09:18,642 --> 00:09:19,852
5, ready.

142
00:09:19,935 --> 00:09:20,936
6, ready.

143
00:09:29,361 --> 00:09:30,863
[Daniel] On your count, Susan.

144
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:34,741
Susan?

145
00:09:42,249 --> 00:09:43,250
Sir.

146
00:09:48,589 --> 00:09:50,591
When we engage the sheriff and his family,

147
00:09:50,674 --> 00:09:53,844
the rest of the fugitives will attempt
to reenter the silo.

148
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:55,804
That's why the ramp will be targeted
with compound.

149
00:09:55,888 --> 00:09:58,140
But if we let them go back inside,

150
00:09:59,266 --> 00:10:00,684
they wouldn't come out again.

151
00:10:01,476 --> 00:10:03,270
We'd end the rebellion,

152
00:10:03,353 --> 00:10:06,106
eliminate any possibility
of silo-to-silo contact,

153
00:10:06,190 --> 00:10:08,901
and reinforce the Pact's infallibility.

154
00:10:18,035 --> 00:10:20,078
Maintain targets and prepare to engage.

155
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:30,881
[Charlotte] There are women and children
out there, sir.

156
00:10:32,466 --> 00:10:33,717
I won't do it.

157
00:10:48,899 --> 00:10:49,900
You're dismissed.

158
00:11:04,248 --> 00:11:05,541
[Victor sighs]

159
00:11:05,624 --> 00:11:06,625
[sighs]

160
00:11:06,708 --> 00:11:09,211
Let the record reflect the change
in operational command.

161
00:11:16,301 --> 00:11:19,513
The citizens of Silo 17 have chosen
to go outside.

162
00:11:19,596 --> 00:11:21,348
They are beyond the Pact

163
00:11:22,558 --> 00:11:24,893
but they're not outside the Directive.

164
00:11:25,853 --> 00:11:26,854
[pilots] Yes, sir.

165
00:11:29,690 --> 00:11:33,610
Groups 1 and 2,
commence operations on my command.

166
00:11:33,694 --> 00:11:35,529
Group 2, release compound.

167
00:11:35,612 --> 00:11:37,114
[typing]

168
00:11:37,197 --> 00:11:38,407
[gas hissing]

169
00:11:43,829 --> 00:11:45,706
[shouting]

170
00:11:53,130 --> 00:11:55,299
- [Daniel] Show me the air lock.
- [screaming]

171
00:11:58,260 --> 00:12:00,637
Group 1, engage targets.

172
00:12:09,813 --> 00:12:10,814
Make sure.

173
00:12:19,615 --> 00:12:20,616
[sheriff grunting]

174
00:12:26,205 --> 00:12:27,706
Groups 3 and 4, begin.

175
00:12:39,593 --> 00:12:43,055
Groups 5 and 6,
descend through 500 feet. Fire at will.

176
00:12:48,977 --> 00:12:50,729
[screaming continues]

177
00:12:57,528 --> 00:12:58,529
Switch to thermal.

178
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:14,169
[screaming continues]

179
00:13:17,089 --> 00:13:18,298
Let's cut the audio.

180
00:13:18,799 --> 00:13:20,008
- [beep]
- [audio ends]

181
00:13:39,111 --> 00:13:41,154
All right, which way is that wind going?

182
00:13:41,238 --> 00:13:44,575
Group 3, secondary sweep,
southeast quadrant.

183
00:13:44,658 --> 00:13:46,869
Group 5, seeing that? Runners at 2:00.

184
00:13:47,452 --> 00:13:48,620
Can we punch in on that?

185
00:13:50,414 --> 00:13:51,582
All right, live target update?

186
00:13:52,207 --> 00:13:54,668
[pilot] 2,453, sir.

187
00:13:54,751 --> 00:13:56,128
Let's get that number down.

188
00:15:21,129 --> 00:15:24,591
The pilots I've debriefed so far
seem almost exhilarated.

189
00:15:25,259 --> 00:15:26,885
I may have underestimated their...

190
00:15:27,970 --> 00:15:28,971
What?

191
00:15:29,972 --> 00:15:31,348
I don't know, their...

192
00:15:32,182 --> 00:15:33,600
We're professionals, Victor.

193
00:15:34,393 --> 00:15:35,811
This is what we trained for.

194
00:15:35,894 --> 00:15:39,273
Yeah. You... You're something more, Troy.

195
00:15:40,357 --> 00:15:41,775
I serve at the director's pleasure.

196
00:15:41,859 --> 00:15:42,985
We all do.

197
00:15:43,735 --> 00:15:45,779
- Doug. Randy.
- [knocks on door]

198
00:15:47,447 --> 00:15:49,032
Madam Director.

199
00:15:49,116 --> 00:15:52,119
Welcome, old friend.
It's been several shifts.

200
00:15:52,202 --> 00:15:53,245
You look wonderful.

201
00:15:53,328 --> 00:15:56,874
Yeah? I feel like hell. I'll never get
used to being rapid-sequenced.

202
00:15:56,957 --> 00:15:59,084
[kisses] I apologize.

203
00:15:59,168 --> 00:16:01,003
- Well, it couldn't be helped.
- Hmm.

204
00:16:01,086 --> 00:16:03,922
Sit, please. I've already had my grits,
I'm afraid.

205
00:16:04,006 --> 00:16:05,591
But can I offer you tea?

206
00:16:05,674 --> 00:16:08,510
Tea. Ah, that would be wonderful.
You're very kind.

207
00:16:08,594 --> 00:16:12,639
Well, I felt the man of the hour
deserved special recognition.

208
00:16:12,723 --> 00:16:15,100
Now, I'll be mother.

209
00:16:15,184 --> 00:16:16,185
[Victor] Mm-hmm.

210
00:16:16,268 --> 00:16:19,813
I knew when we started this long,
difficult adventure

211
00:16:19,897 --> 00:16:23,567
that I would never make it
without my afternoon tea.

212
00:16:24,401 --> 00:16:26,612
Though supplies are running low.

213
00:16:29,448 --> 00:16:30,449
Troy.

214
00:16:31,491 --> 00:16:34,036
I'm awarding you a certificate of merit

215
00:16:34,661 --> 00:16:38,165
for your coolheadedness
and your innovative leadership.

216
00:16:38,248 --> 00:16:41,293
Thank you, ma'am, but I just did my job.

217
00:16:41,376 --> 00:16:43,545
[chuckles] He's so modest.

218
00:16:43,629 --> 00:16:45,005
We've had rebellions before,

219
00:16:45,088 --> 00:16:48,467
but a mass exodus of this scale
is unprecedented.

220
00:16:48,550 --> 00:16:52,888
Your swift, decisive action
prevented a catastrophe.

221
00:16:54,515 --> 00:16:56,892
And you're sure that
there was no contamination?

222
00:16:56,975 --> 00:17:00,896
None. 9,835 fugitives, all accounted for.

223
00:17:00,979 --> 00:17:02,689
How many left alive inside?

224
00:17:02,773 --> 00:17:03,899
No more than a hundred.

225
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:05,901
Are they a threat?

226
00:17:05,983 --> 00:17:07,236
They lost their generator,

227
00:17:07,319 --> 00:17:10,405
so they have no internal power,
no heating, no cooling--

228
00:17:10,489 --> 00:17:12,574
They're still getting
external power in IT.

229
00:17:12,657 --> 00:17:16,203
But to cut that,
we'd have to shut down the sector.

230
00:17:17,329 --> 00:17:20,123
No, without a generator,
their plants and farm stock will die,

231
00:17:20,207 --> 00:17:22,000
and the groundwater will continue to rise.

232
00:17:22,084 --> 00:17:24,211
If they don't starve to death,
they'll drown.

233
00:17:24,294 --> 00:17:27,089
And that boy barricaded in IT,

234
00:17:27,172 --> 00:17:29,258
- is he still alive?
- [Victor] We're not sure.

235
00:17:29,341 --> 00:17:31,468
He had no further
valuable information to give,

236
00:17:31,552 --> 00:17:32,886
so we cut off comms.

237
00:17:32,970 --> 00:17:37,057
Good. Let's keep armed drone surveillance
going for three years

238
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:39,309
just in case any more try to escape.

239
00:17:39,393 --> 00:17:41,103
Five years would be safer.

240
00:17:41,687 --> 00:17:42,855
Five it is.

241
00:17:43,897 --> 00:17:45,899
Now, let's talk about Susan.

242
00:17:45,983 --> 00:17:50,988
You placed her under arrest, Troy,
and I've released her pending an inquiry.

243
00:17:52,573 --> 00:17:55,325
- That's your prerogative, of course.
- Well, that's not good enough.

244
00:17:55,409 --> 00:17:57,703
I asked you here
so you could make your case.

245
00:18:00,539 --> 00:18:03,667
At the time of the incident,
she was operating under my authority,

246
00:18:03,750 --> 00:18:05,335
which flows from the Directive.

247
00:18:05,419 --> 00:18:07,546
But what exactly did she do?

248
00:18:07,629 --> 00:18:08,797
[Daniel] She refused an order,

249
00:18:09,798 --> 00:18:13,385
and then questioned my tactics in front
of pilots under her command.

250
00:18:13,969 --> 00:18:17,097
Her insubordination cost us time,
and could've triggered resistance

251
00:18:17,181 --> 00:18:18,640
from the others, possibly even a revolt.

252
00:18:18,724 --> 00:18:20,559
- But they all did their jobs.
- [Thurman] Good.

253
00:18:20,642 --> 00:18:21,643
No one hesitated.

254
00:18:21,727 --> 00:18:23,854
But the fugitives were about
to breach the berm.

255
00:18:23,937 --> 00:18:25,230
They could've been visible

256
00:18:25,314 --> 00:18:27,524
to the six other silos in their group
within minutes.

257
00:18:27,608 --> 00:18:29,067
Every second counted.

258
00:18:29,151 --> 00:18:31,862
And what do you consider
an appropriate consequence?

259
00:18:39,661 --> 00:18:42,289
May I ask what's laid out
in the Directive?

260
00:18:42,372 --> 00:18:43,707
Neutralization.

261
00:18:44,875 --> 00:18:47,503
But I'm afraid that's not an option.

262
00:18:47,586 --> 00:18:51,798
Look, her conduct was unacceptable,
I agree.

263
00:18:52,299 --> 00:18:54,885
But Susan's skills
will play a critical role

264
00:18:54,968 --> 00:18:57,054
at the end of The Project.

265
00:18:58,222 --> 00:19:00,432
Besides, she's important to my daughter.

266
00:19:00,516 --> 00:19:03,977
Now, I think, perhaps it's best
to just demote her

267
00:19:04,061 --> 00:19:05,562
and put her back to sleep.

268
00:19:06,313 --> 00:19:10,734
Troy, we made you a specialist
for just this kind of emergency.

269
00:19:10,817 --> 00:19:16,490
On behalf of The Project,
I thank you for your exceptional service.

270
00:19:18,992 --> 00:19:20,202
[utensil clinks]

271
00:19:24,665 --> 00:19:25,666
You okay?

272
00:19:27,501 --> 00:19:28,669
She's the director.

273
00:19:30,337 --> 00:19:32,464
And it's a heavy burden.
We need to get you to cryo.

274
00:19:32,548 --> 00:19:34,466
Yeah, listen.

275
00:19:38,595 --> 00:19:40,514
- Can we talk in your office?
- Mm-hmm.

276
00:19:44,309 --> 00:19:46,645
There's a woman.

277
00:19:46,728 --> 00:19:49,189
Hmm. What department does she work in?

278
00:19:49,273 --> 00:19:50,566
She doesn't.

279
00:19:50,649 --> 00:19:52,192
I don't... I don't... [stammers]

280
00:19:52,985 --> 00:19:54,736
I think she might be a memory.

281
00:19:57,114 --> 00:20:00,284
Caught glimpses of her, just flashes,
as I woke up.

282
00:20:00,367 --> 00:20:03,579
When I tried to hang onto them,
they were gone.

283
00:20:09,293 --> 00:20:11,336
I feel like I've raised this
with you before,

284
00:20:12,462 --> 00:20:14,673
seeing this woman when I'm sequenced.

285
00:20:14,756 --> 00:20:16,258
Well, I'd tell you if you had.

286
00:20:21,513 --> 00:20:24,433
She's connected to this somehow.

287
00:20:26,518 --> 00:20:27,519
Oh.

288
00:20:28,729 --> 00:20:30,105
When did that happen?

289
00:20:32,107 --> 00:20:34,401
- No idea.
- And no idea who she is?

290
00:20:34,484 --> 00:20:36,737
No. I hoped you might.

291
00:20:38,363 --> 00:20:39,865
No, I'm sorry.

292
00:20:48,207 --> 00:20:50,501
Look, you have access
to certain records from--

293
00:20:50,584 --> 00:20:52,669
- Troy. Troy.
- Yeah?

294
00:20:52,753 --> 00:20:55,589
The whole purpose and design
of The Project

295
00:20:55,672 --> 00:20:57,257
is to free us from the past.

296
00:20:57,341 --> 00:20:59,510
[stammers] It's best you let this go.

297
00:20:59,593 --> 00:21:01,553
Yeah, whatever you say, Victor.

298
00:21:03,138 --> 00:21:05,766
Even if there was a record,
and even if it survived,

299
00:21:05,849 --> 00:21:07,893
the senator has said this kind of inquiry

300
00:21:07,976 --> 00:21:10,270
- is forbidden by the Directive.
- That's why I'm counting on...

301
00:21:10,354 --> 00:21:12,356
- You can't just--
- ...your discretion, Doctor.

302
00:21:14,525 --> 00:21:17,569
I've proven my value to The Project,
haven't I?

303
00:21:17,653 --> 00:21:19,238
Yes, you have. Beyond any doubt.

304
00:21:19,321 --> 00:21:21,990
Okay, so all I'm asking for is the answer
to one little question.

305
00:21:30,832 --> 00:21:32,376
[scoffs] Please.

306
00:21:38,382 --> 00:21:39,550
[sighs]

307
00:21:46,348 --> 00:21:48,392
I'll have to try and find a pretext

308
00:21:50,269 --> 00:21:51,603
to look into this.

309
00:21:57,192 --> 00:21:58,277
If I do...

310
00:22:00,737 --> 00:22:02,948
I will have it for you next time
you wake up.

311
00:22:04,825 --> 00:22:06,118
I promise.

312
00:22:36,356 --> 00:22:37,357
Be seeing you.

313
00:22:51,997 --> 00:22:53,749
Not if I see you first.

314
00:23:04,134 --> 00:23:05,135
[sighs]

315
00:25:41,375 --> 00:25:43,710
- [explosion]
- [Knox] Come on! Let's go!

316
00:25:46,338 --> 00:25:48,382
[miners grunting]

317
00:25:55,264 --> 00:25:56,890
[grunting continues]

318
00:25:56,974 --> 00:25:59,434
- [Camille] Are the cylinders prepped?
- Prepped and loaded.

319
00:25:59,518 --> 00:26:02,604
Get every raider you can find
and deliver them to the mines now.

320
00:26:02,688 --> 00:26:03,689
Yes, ma'am.

321
00:26:03,772 --> 00:26:05,190
- Emerson.
- Ma'am?

322
00:26:05,274 --> 00:26:07,359
Make sure people see them doing it.

323
00:26:15,534 --> 00:26:16,785
Fuck.

324
00:26:24,960 --> 00:26:26,253
Sit down.

325
00:26:26,336 --> 00:26:28,714
Jo, you know me. I'm not a threat.

326
00:26:28,797 --> 00:26:30,591
I just wanna see my boy.

327
00:26:31,091 --> 00:26:33,177
- That's it.
- [Chad] Submit a request.

328
00:26:33,969 --> 00:26:37,973
I need to say goodbye to my son.

329
00:26:39,600 --> 00:26:41,351
Chad, you have kids.

330
00:26:43,562 --> 00:26:44,605
Please.

331
00:26:47,065 --> 00:26:48,066
I'll ask.

332
00:27:02,956 --> 00:27:05,501
You know, I tried...
I tried to make Camille see, but--

333
00:27:05,584 --> 00:27:07,461
Yeah, yeah, she's hardheaded.

334
00:27:08,212 --> 00:27:10,506
Yeah. You can say that again.

335
00:27:12,758 --> 00:27:14,885
[sighs]

336
00:27:19,056 --> 00:27:20,974
We've done everything we can do, Sims.

337
00:27:21,808 --> 00:27:24,770
We have to trust
that they can get it done.

338
00:27:25,771 --> 00:27:27,022
And if they fail?

339
00:27:30,275 --> 00:27:31,693
[door beeps, opens]

340
00:27:33,111 --> 00:27:34,196
[Camille] Wait.

341
00:27:34,279 --> 00:27:37,908
Wait, you can... you can stop, I'm here.
You can stop the countdown.

342
00:27:37,991 --> 00:27:41,745
My raiders are about to launch
a counteroffensive. Okay? [sniffles]

343
00:27:43,622 --> 00:27:44,831
I'm handling it!

344
00:27:44,915 --> 00:27:47,209
[The Algorithm] <i>You've been given
extraordinary latitude,</i>

345
00:27:47,292 --> 00:27:49,586
<i>but the window of opportunity is closed.</i>

346
00:27:49,670 --> 00:27:51,213
No, no, we're-we're...

347
00:27:51,296 --> 00:27:53,757
We're gassing the mines, okay?

348
00:27:53,841 --> 00:27:56,426
The rebels will be dead in-in minutes.
You can watch.

349
00:27:56,510 --> 00:27:58,303
You can watch on your screens.

350
00:28:00,389 --> 00:28:01,557
Just...

351
00:28:01,640 --> 00:28:04,434
At least let us try! Okay?

352
00:28:04,518 --> 00:28:06,061
<i>Just let us try!</i>

353
00:28:22,369 --> 00:28:23,662
You have five minutes.

354
00:28:27,249 --> 00:28:28,542
That's not enough time.

355
00:28:30,794 --> 00:28:32,880
[groans] That's not enough time.

356
00:28:34,006 --> 00:28:36,216
- That's not enough--
- [The Algorithm] <i>You have five minutes.</i>

357
00:28:51,356 --> 00:28:54,026
Primary and secondary pumps,
armed and locked.

358
00:28:54,109 --> 00:28:56,528
- Valves?
- Primary valve and group valve are open.

359
00:28:56,612 --> 00:28:57,738
Silo valve ready.

360
00:28:57,821 --> 00:29:00,073
Start pressurization sequence.

361
00:29:02,034 --> 00:29:03,619
<i>That's not enough time.</i> [breathes shakily]

362
00:29:05,245 --> 00:29:07,080
[miners] <i>Let's go! Move, move!</i>

363
00:29:07,164 --> 00:29:08,707
Give me that! Give me that!

364
00:29:09,541 --> 00:29:11,210
[grunting]

365
00:29:14,463 --> 00:29:15,631
[miner] Look out!

366
00:29:20,761 --> 00:29:22,221
- Shirl, you good?
- Yeah!

367
00:29:22,304 --> 00:29:24,723
[miner 2] I see the concrete floor!
I need a rebar.

368
00:29:31,188 --> 00:29:33,232
- [grunting]
- [raider] Move, move, move!

369
00:29:33,315 --> 00:29:35,275
- [shouting indistinctly]
- [Shirley] Raiders!

370
00:29:35,359 --> 00:29:37,236
- Fuck! Teddy!
- Huh?

371
00:29:37,319 --> 00:29:38,570
Slow those raiders down.

372
00:29:38,654 --> 00:29:40,531
Nash, Hoover, you're with me.

373
00:29:43,617 --> 00:29:44,993
[panting]

374
00:29:49,581 --> 00:29:52,042
Oh, God. Come on. [sniffles]

375
00:29:53,877 --> 00:29:54,878
Oh, fuck.

376
00:29:55,754 --> 00:29:56,755
[grunts]

377
00:30:00,300 --> 00:30:02,219
[raider speaking indistinctly]

378
00:30:06,223 --> 00:30:08,433
- Drop the tanks! Drop the tanks!
- [shouts]

379
00:30:08,517 --> 00:30:10,018
[grunting]

380
00:30:18,318 --> 00:30:20,070
[grunting, exclaiming]

381
00:30:20,153 --> 00:30:21,238
[Hoover] Get off me!

382
00:30:22,865 --> 00:30:23,907
Get off me!

383
00:30:25,117 --> 00:30:26,159
[raider 2] Don't fucking move!

384
00:30:26,243 --> 00:30:28,996
[raider 1] You got this.
Keep the line moving!

385
00:30:37,462 --> 00:30:38,714
[Knox] Shirl, torch.

386
00:30:41,967 --> 00:30:43,093
I see it.

387
00:30:43,635 --> 00:30:45,220
[grunts] Here.

388
00:30:46,597 --> 00:30:48,640
<i>The raiders are almost in position.</i>

389
00:30:48,724 --> 00:30:50,142
<i>Okay, they're alm...</i>

390
00:30:50,225 --> 00:30:55,022
<i>Just don't... Don't do it, okay?
Don't do it. Please, don't!</i>

391
00:30:57,566 --> 00:30:58,942
<i>Fucking say something!</i>

392
00:30:59,943 --> 00:31:01,153
Say something!

393
00:31:06,033 --> 00:31:07,492
[The Algorithm] <i>Two minutes 15.</i>

394
00:31:15,459 --> 00:31:16,752
[Anthony] Daddy!

395
00:31:17,920 --> 00:31:19,421
Anthony!

396
00:31:35,020 --> 00:31:37,064
- [grunting]
- [Shirley] Come on, come on!

397
00:31:38,023 --> 00:31:39,024
[Knox grunts]

398
00:31:42,569 --> 00:31:44,696
- Come on. Come on!
- [Shirley] Knox?

399
00:31:44,780 --> 00:31:45,781
[grunting]

400
00:31:47,115 --> 00:31:49,493
Shirl, get up here. I need you.

401
00:31:49,576 --> 00:31:51,787
<i>Okay, they-they alm...
They almost have the gas in place.</i>

402
00:31:51,870 --> 00:31:54,831
<i>Okay? The rebels will be dead. Instantly.</i>

403
00:31:54,915 --> 00:31:56,583
<i>We just... We need two minutes.</i>

404
00:31:56,667 --> 00:31:58,335
<i>We need two minutes.</i>

405
00:31:58,418 --> 00:32:00,045
Two minutes, please!

406
00:32:02,756 --> 00:32:03,966
[The Algorithm] <i>Camille,</i>

407
00:32:05,217 --> 00:32:08,929
<i>your failure made a Safeguard necessary.</i>

408
00:32:12,724 --> 00:32:13,767
Fuck!

409
00:32:22,150 --> 00:32:23,151
[Sims chuckles]

410
00:32:30,033 --> 00:32:31,034
Hey, Anthony.

411
00:32:31,660 --> 00:32:33,328
She doesn't wanna hurt you.

412
00:32:34,371 --> 00:32:35,455
Okay?

413
00:32:42,421 --> 00:32:43,922
Where's Mommy?

414
00:32:46,133 --> 00:32:47,885
Mommy's at work.

415
00:32:55,017 --> 00:32:56,602
[Knox grunting]

416
00:33:27,925 --> 00:33:30,093
Sir, did you see that?

417
00:33:30,177 --> 00:33:32,429
- She slipped.
- No, look.

418
00:33:43,899 --> 00:33:44,900
Oxygen.

419
00:33:46,735 --> 00:33:48,695
It's just oxygen. Full pressure!

420
00:33:51,615 --> 00:33:52,741
[Knox grunts]

421
00:33:52,824 --> 00:33:54,368
[grunts] Come on.

422
00:34:02,251 --> 00:34:03,669
Emerson, is it safe?

423
00:34:03,752 --> 00:34:05,420
- [static]
- [Emerson speaking indistinctly]

424
00:34:06,421 --> 00:34:09,507
Say again. Say again. Emerson, is it safe?

425
00:34:10,842 --> 00:34:12,553
Come on. Come on.

426
00:34:20,893 --> 00:34:21,895
[grunting]

427
00:34:22,728 --> 00:34:24,022
Full pressure at silo valve.

428
00:34:25,315 --> 00:34:26,859
Initiate Safeguard.

429
00:34:28,025 --> 00:34:29,194
[tech] On my count.

430
00:34:29,277 --> 00:34:32,906
- In three, two, one.
- Please, just wait. Just wait. Wait.

431
00:34:33,866 --> 00:34:35,242
Please don't.

432
00:34:49,797 --> 00:34:52,384
[alarm blaring]

433
00:34:55,137 --> 00:34:56,179
What's happened?

434
00:34:56,263 --> 00:34:58,390
Sir, the pressure isn't dropping.

435
00:34:59,266 --> 00:35:01,810
- Check again.
- Pressure dipped for one second,

436
00:35:01,894 --> 00:35:03,687
and then immediately returned
to full pressure.

437
00:35:04,855 --> 00:35:06,315
The Safeguard's failed, sir.

438
00:35:18,327 --> 00:35:19,411
[Emerson] <i>It's safe.</i>

439
00:35:23,832 --> 00:35:25,042
[chuckles]

440
00:35:27,211 --> 00:35:29,129
[chuckles] C-Copy. [sniffles]

441
00:35:34,092 --> 00:35:35,552
[sobs]

442
00:35:36,428 --> 00:35:37,679
Oh, fuck.

443
00:35:51,109 --> 00:35:53,445
[both chuckle]

444
00:35:55,489 --> 00:35:56,823
Fuck.

445
00:35:58,450 --> 00:36:00,994
[tech] Sir, we need to depressurize.

446
00:36:01,578 --> 00:36:02,955
[blaring continues]

447
00:36:03,038 --> 00:36:04,039
Sir!

448
00:36:09,837 --> 00:36:11,046
Depressurize.

449
00:36:12,464 --> 00:36:13,757
[beeping]

450
00:36:18,762 --> 00:36:20,472
Where did the Safeguard fail?

451
00:36:21,306 --> 00:36:23,141
[tech] The silo valve was operational.

452
00:36:24,142 --> 00:36:25,227
Somewhere after that.

453
00:36:31,692 --> 00:36:32,901
They capped the pipe.

454
00:36:36,989 --> 00:36:38,156
They capped the pipe.

455
00:36:51,336 --> 00:36:57,759
I want an armed drone in the air
over Silo 18.

456
00:36:59,553 --> 00:37:01,180
Anyone attempts to leave,

457
00:37:02,931 --> 00:37:04,016
kill them.

458
00:37:12,357 --> 00:37:13,525
I need the room.

459
00:37:16,528 --> 00:37:17,613
Clear the room.

460
00:37:19,198 --> 00:37:20,199
Now!

461
00:37:34,838 --> 00:37:36,840
[The Algorithm] <i>That was
a skillful deception.</i>

462
00:37:40,969 --> 00:37:42,804
Wasn't sure you could be deceived.

463
00:37:46,600 --> 00:37:48,519
[The Algorithm]
<i>Your biometrics were stable.</i>

464
00:37:48,602 --> 00:37:49,686
[Camille chuckles]

465
00:37:49,770 --> 00:37:52,147
<i>There was no indication of your betrayal.</i>

466
00:37:52,940 --> 00:37:55,275
Well, you picked me
because I could lie, right?

467
00:37:58,737 --> 00:38:00,364
Why would you lie to me?

468
00:38:08,163 --> 00:38:10,123
I couldn't answer a question.

469
00:38:10,207 --> 00:38:11,750
What question?

470
00:38:12,459 --> 00:38:13,794
<i>Why?</i>

471
00:38:14,795 --> 00:38:16,964
Why do you have the power to kill us?

472
00:38:20,092 --> 00:38:21,343
Asked by whom?

473
00:38:29,226 --> 00:38:30,435
Juliette Nichols.

474
00:38:39,069 --> 00:38:42,906
The human species was
in a terminal cycle of self-annihilation.

475
00:38:47,911 --> 00:38:52,457
The silo was the last best hope
to ensure the survival of the species.

476
00:38:52,541 --> 00:38:58,130
How... How do you ensure survival by
murdering thousands of people at a time?

477
00:39:00,174 --> 00:39:04,595
Questioning the Founders' prerogatives...

478
00:39:07,389 --> 00:39:09,474
- is a violation--
- <i>A violation?</i>

479
00:39:10,684 --> 00:39:13,687
People wanna be free,
so you slaughter them. A violation?

480
00:40:09,368 --> 00:40:10,369
[sighs]

481
00:40:19,378 --> 00:40:21,213
No one goes in, no one goes out. Clear?

482
00:40:21,296 --> 00:40:22,840
- Yes, ma'am.
- [raider] Move. Hey, move, move.

483
00:40:22,923 --> 00:40:24,591
- Hey, hey, hey.
- Hey, man. Hey, get back.

484
00:40:24,675 --> 00:40:26,134
- Whoa.
- You can't approach the prisoners.

485
00:40:26,218 --> 00:40:27,386
They're not prisoners anymore.

486
00:40:27,469 --> 00:40:29,680
- What happened?
- We found the pipe and shut it down.

487
00:40:29,763 --> 00:40:31,557
- Hey, come on.
- Raiders were sent to stop you.

488
00:40:31,640 --> 00:40:33,475
They got an order to switch sides.

489
00:40:33,559 --> 00:40:35,769
Whose order? Nobody has that authority.

490
00:40:35,853 --> 00:40:37,271
[Camille] It was my order.

491
00:40:50,075 --> 00:40:52,244
Okay. No one's going out to clean.
You're all dismissed.

492
00:40:55,622 --> 00:40:56,790
[Anthony] Mommy.

493
00:40:56,874 --> 00:40:57,875
Anthony.

494
00:40:58,709 --> 00:40:59,710
Hey.

495
00:41:00,210 --> 00:41:01,378
Hey. You okay?

496
00:41:02,963 --> 00:41:03,964
Yeah?

497
00:41:04,673 --> 00:41:05,924
[kisses]

498
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:07,801
You're okay.

499
00:41:08,719 --> 00:41:09,720
You're good?

500
00:41:11,388 --> 00:41:13,223
The water supply is safe.

501
00:41:14,516 --> 00:41:15,559
We did it.

502
00:41:17,436 --> 00:41:18,729
[Knox] You know what this day is?

503
00:41:20,439 --> 00:41:21,648
Freedom Day.

504
00:41:22,149 --> 00:41:23,525
[chuckles]

505
00:41:23,609 --> 00:41:25,611
[chuckles]

506
00:41:26,153 --> 00:41:28,530
The first real Freedom Day we've ever had.

507
00:41:29,031 --> 00:41:31,742
And I can't help thinking
we'd all be dead now

508
00:41:32,701 --> 00:41:34,077
if it wasn't for that...

509
00:41:35,621 --> 00:41:37,039
that son of a bitch.

510
00:41:55,974 --> 00:41:57,100
[knocks on door]

511
00:41:57,184 --> 00:41:58,310
[Victor] Yes?

512
00:42:00,187 --> 00:42:01,355
What did you need, sir?

513
00:42:01,438 --> 00:42:04,149
Have them wake Troy for me, please.

514
00:42:04,233 --> 00:42:05,317
Yes, sir.

515
00:42:06,235 --> 00:42:07,319
Thanks, Chloe.

516
00:42:08,320 --> 00:42:09,321
[door closes]

517
00:42:18,080 --> 00:42:21,041
[calm music playing]

518
00:42:28,799 --> 00:42:30,050
[sighs]

519
00:42:37,683 --> 00:42:38,684
[chuckles]

520
00:42:41,937 --> 00:42:42,938
[chuckles]

521
00:42:48,944 --> 00:42:50,445
[sighs]

522
00:43:20,517 --> 00:43:21,518
[chuckles]

523
00:43:40,954 --> 00:43:42,289
[sniffles, sighs]

524
00:43:49,963 --> 00:43:53,509
[sniffling]

525
00:44:17,282 --> 00:44:18,408
[lock clicks]

526
00:44:39,513 --> 00:44:40,722
[sighs]

527
00:44:45,978 --> 00:44:48,605
Hey, it's Jules. Um...

528
00:44:48,689 --> 00:44:49,773
Anyone there?

529
00:44:53,235 --> 00:44:54,528
[Lukas] <i>Jules?</i>

530
00:44:54,611 --> 00:44:57,781
[sighs] Oh, it's good to hear your voice.

531
00:44:58,407 --> 00:44:59,575
<i>Hey, Lukas.</i>

532
00:45:00,409 --> 00:45:02,327
It's so good to hear yours too.

533
00:45:02,911 --> 00:45:04,830
<i>How are you guys doing? Are you okay?</i>

534
00:45:04,913 --> 00:45:07,249
[chuckles] Uh...

535
00:45:07,332 --> 00:45:08,959
I'm mending. What...

536
00:45:09,543 --> 00:45:12,379
Look, the important thing is
that you disabled the Safeguard.

537
00:45:12,963 --> 00:45:16,633
Well, I didn't. It was Knox and Shirley
and Walker and...

538
00:45:16,717 --> 00:45:20,429
Yeah, everyone helped.
Even Camille. So, yeah, we're good.

539
00:45:20,512 --> 00:45:21,513
<i>I think.</i>

540
00:45:21,597 --> 00:45:23,098
<i>For now, at least.</i>

541
00:45:24,016 --> 00:45:25,934
Yeah, and as long as you don't go outside.

542
00:45:26,018 --> 00:45:29,438
And that thing which shot me
doesn't come back. So...

543
00:45:30,480 --> 00:45:33,442
I'm gonna bring all of you back here,
I promise you that.

544
00:45:35,485 --> 00:45:36,820
<i>I know.</i>

545
00:45:36,904 --> 00:45:38,488
<i>But that day...</i>

546
00:45:38,572 --> 00:45:40,282
- ...is not this day.
- <i>...is not this day.</i>

547
00:45:40,866 --> 00:45:41,950
- <i>I got it.</i>
- [chuckles]

548
00:45:45,871 --> 00:45:47,122
Jules, I've missed you.

549
00:46:00,302 --> 00:46:02,262
And I have found out so much
about the universe

550
00:46:02,346 --> 00:46:04,348
that I would love to bore you with, so...
[chuckles]

551
00:46:05,390 --> 00:46:09,144
<i>I can't wait for you to bore me with that.</i>
[chuckles]

552
00:46:12,898 --> 00:46:14,149
So, I, um...

553
00:46:14,816 --> 00:46:16,902
[sniffles] I need to
do something first, okay?

554
00:46:17,694 --> 00:46:21,740
<i>I can't stop thinking about that door
you found in the Digger Void.</i>

555
00:46:23,909 --> 00:46:25,077
I have to go there.

556
00:46:26,286 --> 00:46:27,788
<i>I need to know where it leads.</i>

557
00:46:39,716 --> 00:46:41,426
[tech] Hey. You with us?

558
00:46:42,427 --> 00:46:44,221
Hello. Hey.

559
00:46:44,888 --> 00:46:47,766
Yeah. There he is. I see you in there.

560
00:46:50,185 --> 00:46:52,688
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Easy, easy, easy.

561
00:46:53,355 --> 00:46:56,817
M-My name's Phil. I-I'm your greeter.
Do you know who you are?

562
00:46:56,900 --> 00:46:58,443
- Do you remember your name?
- Troy.

563
00:46:58,527 --> 00:47:01,446
Troy. Excellent, Troy.
A-And what do you do?

564
00:47:02,197 --> 00:47:03,699
I'm a specialist.

565
00:47:03,782 --> 00:47:05,075
Perfect.

566
00:47:05,158 --> 00:47:08,787
It's been 35 years
since your last assignment.

567
00:47:08,871 --> 00:47:11,582
But l-listen,
we had to rapid-sequence you.

568
00:47:11,665 --> 00:47:13,584
Your core temp is still really low.

569
00:47:13,667 --> 00:47:15,669
We're gonna
administer a thermal flush, okay?

570
00:47:15,752 --> 00:47:17,004
- Fuck.
- I know. I know.

571
00:47:17,087 --> 00:47:18,672
Can you lie back for me? I've got you.

572
00:47:18,755 --> 00:47:20,716
Just go back. All the way back.

573
00:47:20,799 --> 00:47:23,552
You want something to bite on?
There you go.

574
00:47:24,553 --> 00:47:26,555
[Daniel shouting]

575
00:47:31,059 --> 00:47:32,686
[sighs] Where's Victor?

576
00:47:33,187 --> 00:47:36,857
[Phil] Oof, you got me.
He's probably dealing with some situation.

577
00:47:37,482 --> 00:47:38,775
What situation?

578
00:47:38,859 --> 00:47:40,027
[scoffs]

579
00:47:40,110 --> 00:47:41,904
Yeah, you'd think they'd tell us,
wouldn't you?

580
00:47:42,404 --> 00:47:45,032
I mean,
we're the first faces you guys see.

581
00:47:45,115 --> 00:47:47,910
There's no reason we couldn't give you
a speedy wee briefing.

582
00:47:47,993 --> 00:47:49,494
Hey. When you get upstairs,

583
00:47:49,578 --> 00:47:53,999
maybe mention to somebody that,
you know, we're not just cryo monkeys.

584
00:47:54,791 --> 00:47:59,505
We-We manage the defrost,
we handle medical emergencies.

585
00:47:59,588 --> 00:48:01,298
We're skilled professionals.

586
00:48:01,381 --> 00:48:06,386
I know you work with a lot of shifts.
But trust me, our shift, J-7, the best.

587
00:48:06,470 --> 00:48:09,431
Great people, great chemistry,
lots of hustle.

588
00:48:09,515 --> 00:48:12,434
Shift boss can be a bit of a dick
but he's just trying to keep us on point,

589
00:48:12,518 --> 00:48:14,728
making sure we're
all giving the Silo 110%.

590
00:48:14,811 --> 00:48:16,647
And we have amazing parties.
You should come.

591
00:48:16,730 --> 00:48:18,774
People would go nuts to meet the guy
that solved Silo 17--

592
00:48:18,857 --> 00:48:22,778
Troy. Joel, J-7 shift boss.
I'll walk you the rest of the way.

593
00:48:23,362 --> 00:48:24,363
Thanks, Phil.

594
00:48:27,115 --> 00:48:28,909
We came on shift five months ago.

595
00:48:29,743 --> 00:48:32,579
About three months ago,
Silo 18 destabilized.

596
00:48:33,080 --> 00:48:36,208
That was after their sheriff,
Juliette Nichols, was sent out to clean.

597
00:48:36,291 --> 00:48:41,129
Somehow, she got hold of the good tape,
made it over the hill to Silo 17 and back.

598
00:48:44,258 --> 00:48:46,301
Hell, Victor was prepping a Safeguard

599
00:48:46,385 --> 00:48:48,595
when their head of IT threw in
with the rebels.

600
00:48:49,471 --> 00:48:51,974
Bought 'em the time
they needed to cap the pipe.

601
00:48:54,977 --> 00:48:56,311
Where's Victor?

602
00:48:56,395 --> 00:48:58,397
[Joel] Uh, this...
They're trying to locate him.

603
00:48:58,981 --> 00:49:02,943
Uh... We have aerial surveillance,
fully armed and we're making preparations

604
00:49:03,026 --> 00:49:05,737
in case you decide
an external Safeguard is indicated.

605
00:49:05,821 --> 00:49:08,657
- External Safeguard?
- Yeah, what you did in 17.

606
00:49:08,740 --> 00:49:09,741
That's what we call it.

607
00:49:11,159 --> 00:49:12,995
This Juliette Nichols
doesn't sound stupid.

608
00:49:13,078 --> 00:49:16,373
If she saw what happened to 17, she's
probably not gonna let her people go out.

609
00:49:17,583 --> 00:49:19,126
- Yeah.
- [phone rings]

610
00:49:20,169 --> 00:49:21,545
[clears throat] Operations.

611
00:49:22,212 --> 00:49:23,213
Yes.

612
00:49:24,506 --> 00:49:25,507
All right.

613
00:49:25,591 --> 00:49:28,719
Uh... Troy,
Victor's requested you in his quarters.

614
00:49:29,803 --> 00:49:31,638
[Daniel] Let me know if anything changes.

615
00:49:32,222 --> 00:49:33,265
[Joel] Will do.

616
00:49:37,019 --> 00:49:38,937
It can carry this many people, right?

617
00:49:39,021 --> 00:49:40,397
We'll see, won't we?

618
00:49:51,283 --> 00:49:52,576
[Daniel] Victor asked to see me.

619
00:49:53,327 --> 00:49:55,204
- I asked to see you.
- Henry.

620
00:49:56,121 --> 00:49:57,456
This your shift?

621
00:49:57,539 --> 00:50:00,042
No, I was rapid-sequenced, just like you.

622
00:50:00,125 --> 00:50:02,044
What do they need Internal Security for?

623
00:50:02,711 --> 00:50:04,004
[sighs]

624
00:50:16,058 --> 00:50:17,059
Fuck.

625
00:50:17,935 --> 00:50:18,936
[Henry] Yeah.

626
00:50:20,395 --> 00:50:21,396
[Daniel sighs]

627
00:50:21,480 --> 00:50:23,232
[sighs] We don't want this getting out.

628
00:50:23,315 --> 00:50:24,775
No, of course not.

629
00:50:25,943 --> 00:50:27,152
[Henry sighs]

630
00:50:29,696 --> 00:50:30,739
You okay?

631
00:50:31,865 --> 00:50:34,159
[Daniel] Yeah. I mean, yeah.

632
00:50:34,243 --> 00:50:35,994
I just... I don't know what to say.

633
00:50:37,538 --> 00:50:39,873
Founder kills himself. [sighs]

634
00:50:40,791 --> 00:50:42,292
That's a big fucking deal.

635
00:50:42,376 --> 00:50:44,169
Mmm. Did he leave a note?

636
00:50:44,253 --> 00:50:45,921
- Haven't found one.
- Mmm.

637
00:50:46,004 --> 00:50:50,759
But the last thing he ordered before he...
was that you be woken up.

638
00:50:51,760 --> 00:50:56,348
So, I thought you might have some insight
into what was troubling him.

639
00:51:00,185 --> 00:51:03,355
You two worked together many times.

640
00:51:03,438 --> 00:51:07,192
Almost seemed like he wanted
to be on shift when you were.

641
00:51:12,406 --> 00:51:13,949
I have no idea.

642
00:51:14,783 --> 00:51:17,119
I sometimes got the sense that he, uh...

643
00:51:18,453 --> 00:51:22,040
he knew me from before,
but obviously he couldn't say.

644
00:51:22,124 --> 00:51:23,208
No.

645
00:51:35,053 --> 00:51:36,263
He was a good man.

646
00:51:37,139 --> 00:51:39,308
I liked him. I just...

647
00:51:39,975 --> 00:51:42,686
I don't know if I ever really knew him.

648
00:51:47,357 --> 00:51:48,525
[door opens]

649
00:52:05,876 --> 00:52:08,921
[Juliette gasps] Okay.

650
00:52:09,546 --> 00:52:10,589
You guys okay?

651
00:52:12,716 --> 00:52:13,926
Thought you didn't like water.

652
00:52:14,009 --> 00:52:15,260
Yeah, I don't.

653
00:52:15,969 --> 00:52:17,679
And since 17, I hate it.

654
00:52:19,014 --> 00:52:20,307
Okay, so,

655
00:52:20,891 --> 00:52:23,936
Lukas said that he went left
of the digger, so...

656
00:52:26,188 --> 00:52:27,189
- Yeah?
- All right.

657
00:52:42,996 --> 00:52:45,290
[Juliette] Okay, let's go.

658
00:52:54,925 --> 00:52:57,302
Joel, I need to listen to playback
of the conversation

659
00:52:57,386 --> 00:52:58,762
between Victor and Camille Sims.

660
00:52:58,846 --> 00:53:00,764
- Yes, sir.
- And who's on shift in Engineering?

661
00:53:00,848 --> 00:53:02,558
Uh... I'll find out.

662
00:53:02,641 --> 00:53:03,809
Have them standing by.

663
00:53:03,892 --> 00:53:05,602
We're gonna find a way
to Safeguard Silo 18.

664
00:53:05,686 --> 00:53:06,687
Sir.

665
00:53:09,147 --> 00:53:10,148
Troy.

666
00:53:11,191 --> 00:53:13,861
There's activity near 18's Forward Vault.

667
00:53:13,944 --> 00:53:14,945
Really?

668
00:53:16,029 --> 00:53:17,489
- Put it up.
- [Joel] You got it.

669
00:53:32,171 --> 00:53:34,840
[Hank] So, what now?

670
00:53:37,176 --> 00:53:40,596
[Juliette] Lukas said he just touched it.

671
00:53:48,562 --> 00:53:49,813
[The Algorithm] <i>Juliette Nichols.</i>

672
00:53:49,897 --> 00:53:52,649
<i>Do not attempt at
any further investigation.</i>

673
00:53:53,358 --> 00:53:54,359
Why?

674
00:53:54,860 --> 00:53:56,486
What are you afraid we'll find?

675
00:53:57,196 --> 00:53:58,947
[The Algorithm]
<i>Return above the digger barrier...</i>

676
00:53:59,031 --> 00:54:01,825
and do not attempt to investigate further.

677
00:54:02,784 --> 00:54:04,661
<i>What will happen if we don't?</i>

678
00:54:05,204 --> 00:54:08,040
Every living thing in your silo will die.

679
00:54:08,123 --> 00:54:11,335
<i>You've already tried that and failed.
And we know you're gonna keep trying.</i>

680
00:54:11,418 --> 00:54:12,419
<i>So</i>

681
00:54:13,128 --> 00:54:14,630
<i>what do we have to lose?</i>

682
00:54:17,257 --> 00:54:18,258
[sighs]

683
00:54:27,309 --> 00:54:31,396
[The Algorithm] <i>As long as you make
no attempt to contact another silo,</i>

684
00:54:32,147 --> 00:54:33,982
<i>there will be no Safeguard.</i>

685
00:54:34,900 --> 00:54:36,360
You're offering us a deal?

686
00:54:40,489 --> 00:54:41,782
A compromise.

687
00:54:42,407 --> 00:54:43,867
<i>A compromise?</i> [scoffs]

688
00:54:47,496 --> 00:54:48,497
That's fair.

689
00:54:51,625 --> 00:54:52,626
We accept.

690
00:54:59,716 --> 00:55:01,635
Okay. Let's go.

691
00:55:12,938 --> 00:55:14,189
[typing]

692
00:55:15,607 --> 00:55:17,067
[beeping]

693
00:55:49,391 --> 00:55:51,643
Wait, can we just... What the fuck was that?
Will you just stop?

694
00:55:51,727 --> 00:55:53,937
Hey, shh! Hey.

695
00:55:56,356 --> 00:55:57,941
[Hank] What the fuck just happened?

696
00:55:58,025 --> 00:55:59,776
You don't really believe they'll stop,
do you?

697
00:55:59,860 --> 00:56:01,153
No. Of course not.

698
00:56:03,572 --> 00:56:04,573
Okay, so,

699
00:56:05,449 --> 00:56:07,242
we know they can't Safeguard us.

700
00:56:07,326 --> 00:56:09,369
Yeah, but they are gonna do something.

701
00:56:09,453 --> 00:56:11,788
If they attack from above,
we'll see them coming.

702
00:56:11,872 --> 00:56:13,373
They could drill underground.

703
00:56:13,999 --> 00:56:16,585
Punch a hole through the outer wall
of the Silo, deliver the poison.

704
00:56:16,668 --> 00:56:18,253
We wouldn't know
until they were almost here.

705
00:56:18,337 --> 00:56:22,883
It might be easier than that. That door,
they could get poison in through there.

706
00:56:22,966 --> 00:56:24,051
We could weld it shut.

707
00:56:24,134 --> 00:56:26,428
Or we put a bunch of guys
with guns watching it.

708
00:56:26,512 --> 00:56:30,349
No. But all the other silos,
they face the same threat.

709
00:56:30,432 --> 00:56:31,767
- And what? You wanna warn them?
- No.

710
00:56:31,850 --> 00:56:33,227
I mean, they told us not to do that.

711
00:56:33,310 --> 00:56:35,062
There's no way to do that anyways.

712
00:56:35,145 --> 00:56:37,898
Look, we need to focus on our survival.

713
00:56:37,981 --> 00:56:38,982
Right?

714
00:56:40,651 --> 00:56:42,319
That's what they're expecting us to do.

715
00:56:46,532 --> 00:56:50,953
They're expecting us to prepare
to defend ourselves, right?

716
00:56:51,662 --> 00:56:56,458
Which means they won't be prepared
to defend themselves against us.

717
00:56:58,710 --> 00:57:03,048
So, if we get to them first,
we could protect everyone.

718
00:57:08,095 --> 00:57:09,930
We need to take out Silo 1.

719
00:57:46,049 --> 00:57:47,050
<i>Hello, Troy.</i>

720
00:57:49,428 --> 00:57:52,514
<i>By now you're aware that
I've taken myself off shift.</i>

721
00:57:54,016 --> 00:57:55,225
<i>Permanently.</i>

722
00:58:01,190 --> 00:58:03,066
<i>You don't need to know all the reasons.</i>

723
00:58:05,777 --> 00:58:07,196
<i>I'll just say that</i>

724
00:58:07,988 --> 00:58:11,241
<i>when our attempted Safeguard
of Silo 18 failed,</i>

725
00:58:13,160 --> 00:58:14,328
<i>I realized...</i>

726
00:58:16,413 --> 00:58:17,581
<i>more than anything...</i>

727
00:58:19,708 --> 00:58:21,084
<i>I was relieved.</i>

728
00:58:27,716 --> 00:58:28,884
<i>The last time we talked,</i>

729
00:58:29,927 --> 00:58:31,678
<i>you asked me about a woman.</i>

730
00:58:33,514 --> 00:58:35,265
<i>And I made you a promise.</i>

731
00:58:38,101 --> 00:58:40,312
<i>Her name is Helen Drew.</i>

732
00:59:07,506 --> 00:59:08,549
[exhales shakily]

733
00:59:14,012 --> 00:59:15,389
Helen Drew.

734
00:59:17,266 --> 00:59:18,267
[gasps]

